

API: An API is a set of rules and protocols that allows one
software application to interact with another.
It defines how requests and responses should be structured.
Client-Server Architecture

   incoming http request
client -> -> ->  Server 


Restraunt System

You(Client) -> place order (API request)
the Kitchen(the server)-> prepares the food(process the request)
the waiter(the API)-> brings the food back to you(API response)

Basic API workflow:
-> Client(user/App) sends a request 
-> API process the request
-> Server retrives data or executes logic 
-> API returns a response to the client


REST:Representational State Transfer


State - data
Representational - formats of data(XML, JSON, YAML, HTML etc)
Transfer - carrying the data between cosumer and provider using
            HTTP protocol
            
Key concepts:
i)Resource - subresource
ii)URI    

/home - home.html
/about - about.html  


CMS - 

/post/id/comments 
      

HTTP methods: 
HTTP verbs

GET - to get resource/collection of resources
POST - to create a new resource
PUT -  to update an existing resource/collection of resources (compltely)
PATCH - to update an existing resource/collection of resources(partially)
DELETE - to delete an existing resource or collection of resources


HTTP Status codes:

XXX - three digt number

1XX - Information
2XX - Success(200,201)
3XX - Redirect (301)
4XX - Client side error(400, 401, 403, 404)
5XX - Server side error(500)


Layers: Entity/model, repository, service, controller

security, exceptions, dto, utility

